{
  "about": "The budget rules the Rust backend and the mock share. `budget` is a workstream's spent counters and budget limits (what is left out is the default, 11 automatic turns and 12 wakes), and what the page shows of them: the budget level (`budget_level` in src-tauri/src/domain/workstream.rs, `budgetLevel` in src/lib/workstreamHold.ts), the counters (`BudgetView::of`, `budgetView`) and, in the page only (`stepsOf`, which has no Rust twin), the steps used and the limit it counts them against. `free` is whether a wake is no automatic step: every fact in it is the review that sent a fix round or the build that went back for one (`wake_is_free` in src-tauri/src/agent/supervisor.rs, `isFreeWake` in src/backend/mockSupervisor.ts), the builds read from the audit. `sequences` start a workstream in a state and apply the person's and the supervisor's actions to it in turn: Allow 5 more, Resume, a change of mode and a hold, with what each leaves and the audit lines it adds (actor, action, detail): `allow_more_steps`, `resume_workstream`, `set_workstream_mode` and `hold_workstream` in src-tauri/src/inbox/workstreams.rs, and `allowMore`, `resume`, `setMode` and `hold` in src/backend/mockWorkstreams.ts. A refused action has `error` and changes nothing.",
